  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3003.12 Sale of Vehicle with A Hardship Registration",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.12 Sale of Vehicle with A Hardship Registration.\n\n(a) A hardship registration shall be terminated in the event the vehicle is sold and the owner does not purchase another vehicle.\n\n(b) Upon receipt of a written request from the owner, the department shall transfer a hardship registration from one vehicle to another in the event the owner sells or trades in the vehicle and immediately purchases a different vehicle.\n\n(c) A hardship registration shall not prohibit the registrant from selling his or her vehicle.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04 (from Saf-C 3003.14); ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
